# Scrappy server settings. Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and uncomment what
# you need — nothing here is required. They're read only on the server, never
# shipped to the browser. Restart the dev server after changing them.
# The README's "Configuration" table lists these too.
#
# There's no AI key here: each person connects their own in the app
# (Settings → AI service). See "Your AI key" in the README.

# ── Development ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# MOCK_AI — answer the AI routes (ingredients, preference, recipes, key check,
#   images) with local fakes: no AI service called, no credit used.
#   Values: 1 = on; unset, 0 or false = off. Default: off.
#   The app still asks for a key (any text works). Special keys and phrases
#   show each failure — see "Mock mode" in the README.
# MOCK_AI=1

# DEV_LAN_ORIGIN — your computer's LAN IP, so a phone on the same Wi-Fi can open
#   the dev server (Next blocks other origins by default; without this the page
#   shows but buttons do nothing). *.trycloudflare.com is always allowed.
#   Values: an IP like 10.0.0.175. Default: unset.
#   Tip: the LAN address stays the same between runs, so a saved AI key stays
#   too; a tunnel address changes every run.
# DEV_LAN_ORIGIN=10.0.0.175

# ── AI service ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ALLOW_PRIVATE_LLM_URLS — let a "Custom" AI service use a private or local
#   address (localhost, 192.168.x.x, 10.x.x.x…). Off by default because
#   requests go through this server: on a public host, a visitor could make it
#   reach machines on the host's own network. Turn on only when you run Scrappy
#   on your own network, e.g. to use Ollama on another machine.
#   Values: 1 = allow; unset, 0 or false = refuse. Default: refuse.
# ALLOW_PRIVATE_LLM_URLS=1

# ── Step pictures (Midjourney) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# No key: sign in once with `pnpm midjourney:auth` (tokens are saved in
# .mcp-auth/). Without it, the Step pictures setting is hidden and cooking is
# text only.

# MIDJOURNEY_MCP_URL — the Midjourney MCP server to use.
#   Values: a URL. Default: https://mcp.midjourney.com/mcp
# MIDJOURNEY_MCP_URL=https://mcp.midjourney.com/mcp

# ── Speech fallback (Deepgram) — switched off ────────────────────────────────

# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY — speech-to-text for browsers without the Web Speech API
#   (Firefox). Only used if DEEPGRAM_FALLBACK_ENABLED is set to true in
#   src/lib/voice.ts; it's false, so Firefox users type instead.
#   Values: a Deepgram API key. Default: unset.
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
